From 75026ab31ec09dad601b78b3b36620544f55ad10 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tangxiangbing <tangxiangbing@contributor>


Date: Thu, 19 Mar 2026 16:08:08 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] BUGFIX Fix memory leak in SQL Filter feature.

Issue:
------
The Sql_filter_record class had a member variable m_key_array of type
std::vector<std::string>, which was populated using boost::split.
boost::split dynamically allocates memory for the vector elements.
However, Sql_filter_record objects are allocated on a MEM_ROOT, so
their destructor is never invoked. Consequently, m_key_array was never
destroyed, causing a memory leak each time throttling was applied.

Solution:
------
To resolve the leak, m_key_array has been removed from the class.
Instead, a local temporary vector is now created on the stack where
needed. This ensures that the memory allocated by boost::split is
properly freed when the vector goes out of scope.
